# Knowledge Curator

An approval-gated Knowledge Curator API for article review and ticket-theme gap analysis.

## Run

```powershell
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m uvicorn Main:app --reload
```

Open the interactive API documentation at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`.

To run the Streamlit shell:

```powershell
python -m streamlit run streamlit_app.py
```

## API

- `GET /health`
- `POST /v1/articles/review`
- `POST /v1/gaps/analyze`
- `POST /v1/articles/upload`
- `POST /v1/architecture/design`
- `POST /v1/approval/handoff`

All generated findings and drafts have `approvalStatus = "PENDING_HUMAN_APPROVAL"`.
There is no publishing endpoint or automatic approval behavior.

## Audit

Local development audit events are stored in `knowledge_curator.db`. The payload and
evidence count are recorded only after an operation is executed.

## Containers

```powershell
docker compose up --build
```

The compose stack starts PostgreSQL, Redis, Qdrant, the API, and Streamlit. Set
`POSTGRES_PASSWORD` and external integration variables before a shared or production
deployment. `.env.example` lists approved integration settings.

## Identity

Development may use `x-user-role` only when `KC_ALLOW_HEADER_AUTH=true`. Production,
UAT, and test require a validated OIDC bearer token and configured issuer, audience,
and JWKS URL.